  "term": "psychological deficit",
  "definition": "A psychological deficit is a supposed fixed shortcoming or impairment in a person’s psychological functioning that is treated as residing within the individual. In this source, the term is used mainly as a contrast, arguing that spiritual bypassing should not be understood in that way.",
